{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI am writing from Kassel, where I arrived this morning at eleven. The town is pleasant, though the air is thick with the dampness of the Rhine valley. I spent the entire afternoon walking the streets, observing the architecture and the faces of the people. There is a quiet dignity here, distinct from the bustle of Berlin. I walked until my feet ached, enjoying the solitude and the change of scenery.\n\nI have dined well, though the wine was not quite up to the standard of our home cellar. I am tired but content. The journey continues, but for now, I rest. I think often of you and the boys. Please give my regards to Karl and Immanuel when you next see them. I hope this letter finds you in good health and high spirits.\n\nYours always,\nG. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080158,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":183,"prompt_tokens":915,"total_tokens":1098,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-C9Qf3LYeEBz30ztrL2XcGcHN3SBAwyCY","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":915,"prompt_ms":998.479,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0912338797814207,"prompt_per_second":916.3938350230701,"predicted_n":183,"predicted_ms":4353.069,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.91796153846154,"predicted_per_second":41.80958307805366}}